WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.800
No new Conditional
Access policy is needed.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.575
Five policies in the workbook's library
already carry the partner tenant list.

3
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:15.125
CA009, for MFA, and CA010, for
terms of use, include partner users.

4
00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:23.325
CA011, CA012 and CA038 apply guest limits
to everyone except the partner tenants.

5
00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:26.032
The list must be identical in all five;

6
00:00:26.032 --> 00:00:29.788
a partner in one and not the
others is a drift finding.

7
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:32.203
The identity governance officer owns it,

8
00:00:32.203 --> 00:00:35.825
and a partner enters it only when
its access package goes live.

9
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:38.450
The user type decides
which policies apply.

10
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.731
CA011, CA012 and CA038 match
only guest-type external users,

11
00:00:43.731 --> 00:00:49.012
so an external member from an
unlisted tenant escapes them.

12
00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:52.350
A member also gets member-level
directory permissions,

13
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.050
and falls outside persona rules
and reviews scoped to guests.

14
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.725
That's why partner persons
are guests by default.

15
00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.579
A read-only Graph check compares
the list across the five policies

16
00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:06.430
and against the partner entries
in cross-tenant access settings.
